# Rclex — Parameters

```elixir
Mix.install(
  [
    {:rclex, github: "FelixPe/rclex"}
  ],
  config: [
    rclex: [
      ros2_message_types: ["std_msgs/msg/String"]
    ]
  ]
)
```

## About

Declare parameters on a node, read/write them locally, and inspect them
remotely with `ros2 param`.

Reference implementations:

* C++ — [ros2/demos · `demo_nodes_cpp/parameters/set_and_get_parameters.cpp`](https://github.com/ros2/demos/blob/rolling/demo_nodes_cpp/src/parameters/set_and_get_parameters.cpp)
* Python — [ros2/demos · `demo_nodes_py/parameters/set_parameters_callback.py`](https://github.com/ros2/demos/blob/rolling/demo_nodes_py/demo_nodes_py/parameters/set_parameters_callback.py)
* See also [`parameter_client.md`](../parameter_client.md) for the remote
  parameter-client API exposed by Rclex.

Verify from another terminal:

```sh
ros2 param list /example/livebook_node
ros2 param get /example/livebook_node my_int
ros2 param set /example/livebook_node my_int 42
```

## Generate

```elixir
Mix.Task.run("rclex.gen", [])
Application.stop(:rclex)
Application.unload(:rclex)
{:ok, _} = Application.ensure_all_started(:rclex)
:ok
```

## Declare and read parameters

```elixir
Rclex.start_node("livebook_node", namespace: "/example")

:ok =
  Rclex.declare_parameter("livebook_node", "my_int",
    namespace: "/example",
    default_value: 7,
    description: "An example integer parameter."
  )

:ok =
  Rclex.declare_parameter("livebook_node", "my_string",
    namespace: "/example",
    default_value: "hello"
  )

{:ok, value} = Rclex.get_parameter("livebook_node", "my_int", namespace: "/example")
IO.puts("my_int = #{inspect(value)}")
```

## Update from inside the notebook

```elixir
:ok =
  Rclex.set_parameter("livebook_node", "my_int", 42,
    namespace: "/example"
  )

{:ok, new_value} = Rclex.get_parameter("livebook_node", "my_int", namespace: "/example")
IO.puts("my_int is now #{inspect(new_value)}")
```

## Watch for changes

A second cell can subscribe to parameter-event notifications. The handler
needs its own client node.

```elixir
Rclex.start_node("param_watcher")

Rclex.start_parameter_event_handler(
  fn event -> IO.inspect(event, label: "[param event]") end,
  "param_watcher"
)
```

## Cleanup

```elixir
Rclex.stop_parameter_event_handler("param_watcher")
Rclex.stop_node("param_watcher")
Rclex.stop_node("livebook_node", namespace: "/example")
```
